## Findings on cut-v5d (the baseline the round-2 cut is compared with)
1. **s17 and s18 (1:42.4–1:53.1) judder as the objective says**: whole-pixel steps, held frames every 3–9 frames
   (25 + 13 held frames, 4 jump events). Both are to be replaced by Wan/Gemini shots; if any push on them remains it has
   to pass the threshold below.
2. **s09 at 0:48–0:51 (dp's model shot, EDL has no zoom or speed on it so the conform passes it through unchanged)**:
   not whole-pixel judder. The push is fast and even (2.0–2.5 px/f at the corners, ripple 0.021, no repeated frame); what
   is measurable is a period-of-4-frames dip of about 10% of the speed (every 4th frame from about 0:48.2 to 0:50.5, median depth 0.90;
   7% of frames >10% off). That is a 6 fps cadence in the generated shot itself, so it is in dp's file, not in the conform.
   It is mild; I measure it as a smoothness residue, not as the step pattern of s17/s18.
3. **Other stills with a push, speed ripple ≥ 0.1 with 20–45% of frames >10% off, no held frame** (sub-pixel but choppy; period-3
   dips to ~0.7× speed): s10.1 0.17 (0:53.5), s10.2 0.27 (0:55.0), s12.2 0.15 (1:06.3), s13a 0.073 with period-3 dips
   (1:12.1–1:19.8), s14.2 0.11 (1:28.1), s16.2 0.12 (1:37.3), s16.3 0.15 (1:39.8), the s19 sky tail 0.21 (1:57.0–1:58.8).
   Smooth: s12.3 0.024, s12.4 0.016, s16.1 0.027, s14.1 0.040, s15.3 0.048.
4. **Conform judder in model shots slowed by `speed`** (repeated frames, no blend): s04 (speed 0.76/0.77) 10 + 18 held
   frames at 0:15.5–0:21.3, s05 (0.96) 5, s03 (0.98) 2. Owner: editor (conform). Mild, single repeated frames; fix by
   leaving them at speed 1 or frame-blending the retime.
5. Measurement-limited (speed below 0.3 px/f, ripple not meaningful): s04, s06, s13a_strike.
6. Title card 1:59.1–2:01.8 is static by design (ripple 0, 19 identical frames).

