## Pass/fail rule I will apply to every round-2 cut (spec 16–17)
- A move passes when its speed ripple ≤ 0.05 **and** it has no repeated frame inside it **and** no jump event; a
  generated shot with a fixed cadence ripple (like s09) is reported with its numbers and the owner (dp), and judged by the
  director whether it is acceptable; > 0.1 or any held frame inside a push is a fault (owner: editor for a still or a conform
  move, dp for a model shot, tested by whether the EDL applies a zoom/speed to it).
- "Moves, not a still with a push" is checked per shot on frames (a contact sheet over the slot) as well as by the content residual.
- Unchanged elsewhere: length, story, audio checks from `qc/cut-v5d/report.md`.
